<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Describing a shear</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Rectangle ABCD, with \(A({@A0[1]@},\,{@A0[2]@})\), \(B({@B0[1]@},\,{@B0[2]@})\), \(C({@C0[1]@},\,{@C0[2]@})\) and \(D({@D0[1]@},\,{@D0[2]@})\), is mapped onto \(A'B'C'D'\), with \(A'({@A1[1]@},\,{@A1[2]@})\), \(B'({@B1[1]@},\,{@B1[2]@})\), \(C'({@C1[1]@},\,{@C1[2]@})\) and \(D'({@D1[1]@},\,{@D1[2]@})\), by a shear.</p><p>(a) The invariant axis is</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) The shear factor is</p><div>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) The area of \(A'B'C'D'\) is</p><div>[[input:ans3]] square units [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) Every [[if test="is(ax=\"x\")"]]y[[else]]x[[/if]]-coordinate stays the same, so the points slide parallel to the [[if test="is(ax=\"x\")"]]x[[else]]y[[/if]]-axis: the [[if test="is(ax=\"x\")"]]x[[else]]y[[/if]]-axis is invariant.</p><p>(b) C is \({@dist@}\) units from the [[if test="is(ax=\"x\")"]]x[[else]]y[[/if]]-axis and moves \({@abs(mv)@}\) units in the [[if test="is(mv<0)"]]negative[[else]]positive[[/if]] [[if test="is(ax=\"x\")"]]x[[else]]y[[/if]]-direction, a signed distance of \({@mv@}\). So the shear factor is \({@mv@} \div {@dist@} = {@k@}\).</p><p>(c) A shear keeps the base and the height, so the area is unchanged: \({@ar@}\) square units. (The determinant of a shear matrix is 1.)</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* Design: describe the transformation from coordinates. Source: adapted from SMP Book 5 (Metric), Chapter 13, Exercise D, question 1. C's distance from the invariant axis is not 0 or 1; the diagnostics (distance moved, -k, 1/k; |k| x area, (1 + |k|) x area) are distinct on every entry. */
slist: [["x",3/2,[[0,2],[4,2],[4,5],[0,5]]],["y",-5/2,[[2,0],[6,0],[6,2],[2,2]]],["x",1/2,[[-2,1],[1,1],[1,3],[-2,3]]],["y",3,[[3,2],[7,2],[7,4],[3,4]]],["x",-1/2,[[-2,2],[2,2],[2,6],[-2,6]]],["y",5/2,[[1,1],[4,1],[4,5],[1,5]]],["x",-3/2,[[2,3],[5,3],[5,7],[2,7]]],["y",4,[[3,3],[6,3],[6,7],[3,7]]],["x",-3/4,[[-2,2],[2,2],[2,5],[-2,5]]],["y",1/4,[[3,0],[7,0],[7,2],[3,2]]]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
ax: slist[ix][1]; k: slist[ix][2]; V: slist[ix][3];
Sm: if ax="x" then matrix([1,k],[0,1]) else matrix([1,0],[k,1]);
imv(v) := list_matrix_entries(Sm.transpose(matrix(v)));
A0: V[1]; B0: V[2]; C0: V[3]; D0: V[4]; A1: imv(A0); B1: imv(B0); C1: imv(C0); D1: imv(D0);
dist: if ax="x" then C0[2] else C0[1];
mv: k*dist;
ar: abs((B0[1]-A0[1])*(D0[2]-A0[2])) + abs((B0[2]-A0[2])*(D0[1]-A0[1]));
opt1: [["neither",false,"neither axis"],["x",is(ax="x"),"the x-axis"],["y",is(ax="y"),"the y-axis"]];
oax: if ax="x" then "y" else "x";
mk: -k; ik: 1/k; aK: abs(k)*ar; aK1: (1+abs(k))*ar;
kw: k+1/3; arw1: ar+1; arw2: ar+5;
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
