  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Matrices and Transformations: describing a shear</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 2.1: Identify the invariant axis and shear factor of a shear from a rectangle and its image, and state the area of the image.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 13, Exercise D, Question 1 of School Mathematics Project, SMP Book 5 (Metric), ed. P. G. Bowie, Cambridge University Press, 1969: coordinates given instead of a tracing, new rectangles and factors, randomised, with named feedback.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
